---
title: Butternut Squash Soup with Crème Fraîche and Fried Sage
servings: 6
prepTime: 20 minutes
cookTime: 75 minutes
difficulty: Medium
Rating: 10/10
description: Roasting butternut squash makes it easier to cut and peel—and also deepens its flavor—in this recipe for a comforting soup that's flavored with fresh sage. Use a spoon to gently swirl the crème fraîche into each bowl of soup for a pretty presentation.
source.name: Williams-sonoma.com
source.url: https://www.williams-sonoma.com/recipe/butternut-squash-soup-with-creme-fraiche-and-fried-sage.html
tags: Soups, Vegetables
---

Preheat an oven to 400°F.

Using the tip of a paring knife, prick each @butternut squash{2}(large, 1.5-2.0 lb each) several times. 
Place the whole squashes on a #baking sheet{} and roast until tender and a knife penetrates the skin easily, about ~{1%hour}.

While the squash is roasting, make the fried sage. 
In a #small fry pan{} over medium-high heat, warm the @olive oil{1/4%cup}.
Add @sage leaves{12}(whole, fresh) and cook until dark green and crispy, ~{30-60%seconds}.
Using a slotted spoon, transfer the fried sage leaves to a paper towel-lined plate. Set aside.

Remove the squash from the oven.
When cool enough to handle, cut in half lengthwise and remove and discard the seeds and fibers.
Scoop the pulp into a bowl and set aside.

In a #saucepan over low heat, melt the @unsalted butter{6%tbsp}.
Add the @yellow onions{2}(chopped) and @sage leaves{4}(fresh, chopped) and cook, stirring occasionally,
until the onions are tender and translucent, ~{8-10%minutes}.
Add the @chicken broth{6%cups}(or vegetable broth) and squash pulp, increase the heat to high and bring to a boil.
Reduce the heat to low and simmer for a few minutes to combine the flavors. Remove from the heat.

Working in batches, using a blender, puree the soup until smooth.
Return to a clean saucepan and reheat gently over medium-low heat.
Stir in the @ground nutmeg{pinch}(fresh grated) and season with #salt and #pepper.

= Serving =
Ladle the soup into warmed bowls.
Top each serving with a few grinds of #pepper, a dollop of @Crème fraîche{} and 2 of the fried sage leaves.
Serve with #crusty baguette slices{} if you like. Serve immediately.
